ask_count >= max_tasks` gate).\n\n**Phases B/C — differential tests** (`tests/`, 89 tests)\n\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and compared byte-for-byte on return values, all 256 description bytes of every `Task`, `stdout`, `stderr`, and the resulting log files. Each scenario gets a *private copy* of each `.so` so the `log_file` static is genuinely fresh (glibc keys loaded objects on inode). Unchecked-pointer rows are compared by forked-child termination status.\n\n**One real divergence found and fixed**\n\nThe C never null-checks a parameter, so NULL gives a raw `SIGSEGV`. The Rust `.so` instead aborted with `SIGABRT` plus `null pointer dereference occurred` on stderr — `debug-assertions` injects `ub_checks` the C compiler has no equivalent of. Fixed in `Cargo.toml` by disabling `debug-assertions`/`overflow-checks` in both profiles; six rows now match exactly.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **`cargo test` never builds this crate's `.so`.** A `cdylib`-only lib target isn't linkable by the test harness, so cargo skips it — my tests were initially running against an artifact from an earlier `cargo build`, and the release run had no `.so` at all. I added a staleness guard in the harness (asserts every `src/*.rs` is older than the `.so`) and made `run_verification.sh` build before testing. Worth knowing if you run `cargo test` by hand.\n\n- **Two `ERRORS.md` rows cannot be compared by status, and I did not pretend otherwise.** `finalize_logger` `fclose`s without resetting `log_file`, so calling it twice is use-after-free. Running the *unmodified C library alone* three times gives `0`, `134`, `0` — it's allocator-state dependent, so there is no C-defined result to match. I pinned these structurally instead (exactly one assignment to the static; all four consumers guard on the raw pointer), which is what actually rules out the plausible wrong translation — a defensive `log_file = NULL` — and the mutation check confirms that mutation is caught.\n\nTo guard against a vacuous suite, `mutation_check.sh` injects 20 plausible translation mistakes; all 20 are detected. One (`as isize as usize` → `as u32 as usize`) is dynamically an equivalent mutant — both sign- and zero-extension request sizes that fail on any realistic host — so it's pinned by a structural assertion rather than a value comparison.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (only `build/` added, as instructed).","ttft_ms":3068,"ttft_stream_ms":2904,"time_to_request_ms":46,"type":"result","duration_ms":2572982,"uuid":"a66f55a1-2328-42e4-b97e-dd09a19e9974","queued_turn_count":0}
